  "title": "Darkness",
  "heading": "Darkness",
  "description": "Darkness in art: From 19th century landscape gardens to Anish Kapoor.",
  "source_encoding": "utf-8",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Darkness",
      "links": [],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Egyptian Philosophers have stated the hidden truth of their Theology; they found that according to certain Egyptian writings there is One Principle of all things, which is praised under the name of the Unknown Darkness, thrice repeated.",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Damascius: De Principiis, Vol. 3.\n\n(Early Sixth Century CE.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "[Paris, 1991, p. 167]",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/darkness/Smithson69TMusOTVoid-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "298",
      "height": "390",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Robert Smithson:\n\n\"The Museum of the Void\", 1969",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comme tu me plairait, ô nuit ! sans ces étoiles\n\nDont la lumière parle un langage connu !\n\nCar je cherche le vide, et le noir et le nu !",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Mais les ténèbres sont elles-mêmes des toiles\n\nOù vivent, jaillissant de mon oeil par milliers,\n\nDes êtres disparus aux regards familiers.",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Charles Baudelaire: \"Obsession.\"\n\nLes fleurs du mal (2nd ed.), 1861.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/darkness/ypeij-grot-ingang-zoom-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "227",
      "height": "220",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/darkness/ypeij-grot-zwart-220.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "220",
      "height": "220",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/darkness/ypeij-grot-uitgang-zoom-s.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "213",
      "height": "220",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lucas Pietersz. Roodbaard: Cave in Bos Ypeij, Tytsjerk (the Netherlands), 1850\n\n[entrance, inside, exit]",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/darkness/14-HM-Porte-FenetreAColliou.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": "300",
      "height": "390",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Henri Matisse:\n\nPorte-Fenêtre à Colllioure,\n\n1914",
      "links": []
    },
    {
